{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2422 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "e5bee640680f80cbcc1ea5580541cfb5aa210dc7fd54974de9b24e0b9fd7cdf9" :edb/db-before-t 2421 :edb/db-after-t 2422 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535734 50 #inst "2026-10-09T06:10:15.741Z" 13194139535734 true] [17592186217200 1020 #edb/ref 17592186363888 13194139535734 true] [17592186217200 1020 #edb/ref 17592186363924 13194139535734 true] [17592186217721 1017 #edb/ref 17592186216420 13194139535734 false] [17592186217721 1017 #edb/ref 17592186216424 13194139535734 false] [17592186217721 1017 #edb/ref 17592186363855 13194139535734 true] [17592186217721 1017 #edb/ref 17592186363860 13194139535734 true] [17592186217721 1017 #edb/ref 17592186363865 13194139535734 true] [17592186217721 1017 #edb/ref 17592186363870 13194139535734 true] [17592186217721 1017 #edb/ref 17592186363875 13194139535734 true] [17592186217721 1017 #edb/ref 17592186363880 13194139535734 true] [17592186217721 1017 #edb/ref 17592186363884 13194139535734 true] [17592186217721 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535734 true] [17592186217721 1100 "Suppose we would like to find an integrating factor to convert the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+xy\\,\\text{d}y=0,\\,y>0\n$$\n\ninto an exact equation using an integrating factor. Select the correct options in the reasoning below. For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}=h(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $h(y)$ is independent of $x,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(y)={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\operatorname{exp}⁡(y)$ denotes the exponential function ${e}^{y}.$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)={y}^{3},\\,Q(x,y)=xy.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\,{{field-3}}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\,{{field-4}}\n$$\n\nSince for this equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})={{field-5}},\n$$\n\nwhich depends on $y$ only, then an integrating factor for our equation is\n\n$$\nI(y)={{field-6}}.\n$$\n\nand we arrive at the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-7}}.\n$$" 13194139535734 true] [17592186217721 1100 "Suppose we would like to find an integrating factor to convert the differential equation\n$y^{3}dx + xydy = 0, y > 0$\ninto an exact equation using an integrating factor. Select the correct options in the reasoning below. For a differential equation of the form\n$P(x, y)dx + Q(x, y)dy = 0$,\nwe have that if\n\n$\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y} - \\frac{∂Q}{∂x})$ {{field-1}}\n\nwhere $h(y)$ is independent of $x$, then an integrating factor for the equation is\n$\\exp (∫h(x)dy)$ {{field-2}}\nwhere $\\exp (y)$ denotes the exponential function $e^{y}$." 13194139535734 false] [17592186217721 1145 "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=h(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $h(y)$ is independent of $x,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(y)=\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-\\int h(y)\\,\\text{d}y)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\operatorname{exp}⁡(y)$ denotes the exponential function ${e}^{y}.$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)={y}^{3},\\,Q(x,y)=xy.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{3})=3{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}) & =\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}(3{y}^{2}-y) \\\\  & =3{y}^{-1}-{y}^{-2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis a function of $y$ only, we can conclude that an integrating factor for our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(y) & =\\operatorname{exp}⁡(\\int -(3{y}^{-1}-{y}^{-2})\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1/y)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{exp}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡{y}^{-3})\\cdot \\operatorname{exp}⁡(-1/y) \\\\  & ={y}^{-3}\\,{e}^{-1/y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand by multiplying our differential equation by the integrating factor, we have\n\n$$\nI(y)\\cdot ({y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+xy\\,\\text{d}y)=I(y)\\cdot 0\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n{y}^{-3}{e}^{-1/y}({y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+xy\\,\\text{d}y)=0.\n$$" 13194139535734 true] [17592186363855 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363856 13194139535734 true] [17592186363855 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363857 13194139535734 true] [17592186363855 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363858 13194139535734 true] [17592186363855 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363859 13194139535734 true] [17592186363855 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535734 true] [17592186363855 1041 "field-1" 13194139535734 true] [17592186363855 1104 #edb/ref 17592186363858 13194139535734 true] [17592186363855 1110 #uuid "19f56030-70b0-53de-8412-017518ed00a3" 13194139535734 true] [17592186363856 1034 "\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})" 13194139535734 true] [17592186363856 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535734 true] [17592186363856 1111 #uuid "742142fe-a809-51e1-a21e-caed9a8824f4" 13194139535734 true] [17592186363857 1034 "\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})" 13194139535734 true] [17592186363857 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535734 true] [17592186363857 1111 #uuid "8de55fd6-e980-5a5f-935b-26153c3d9ae1" 13194139535734 true] [17592186363858 1034 "\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})" 13194139535734 true] [17592186363858 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535734 true] [17592186363858 1111 #uuid "0079b171-8e72-54e1-bdc9-bda6fe1be762" 13194139535734 true] [17592186363859 1034 "\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})" 13194139535734 true] [17592186363859 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535734 true] [17592186363859 1111 #uuid "4596363c-10cd-55be-8655-b89396c561f3" 13194139535734 true] [17592186363860 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363861 13194139535734 true] [17592186363860 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363862 13194139535734 true] [17592186363860 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363863 13194139535734 true] [17592186363860 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363864 13194139535734 true] [17592186363860 1040 #e